.TITLE "cat"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Concatenates and displays the content of files. It is primarily used to __read__ small files or __combine__ multiple files into one.

.DIV "TLDR"
**cat file**
Displays the entire content of a file in the terminal.
> __file__ the target file

**cat file1 file2**
Combines and displays the contents of multiple files in sequence.
> __file1__ first file | __file2__ second file

**cat -n file**
Displays the content of a file with line numbers.
> __-n__ number lines flag | __file__ the target file

**cat -s file**
Suppresses multiple consecutive blank lines into a single blank line.
> __-s__ squeeze flag | __file__ the target file

.DIV "SUMMARY"
While __cat__ is convenient for reading files, for larger files, consider using __less__ to avoid cluttering your terminal. You can also use __cat__ with redirection (>) to quickly create or overwrite files with new content.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**linux:tail** **linux:head**

